        "accordion_ibjhmw": {
          "type": "accordion",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Health Benefits",
            "content": "<p>Get ready to experience a full body reset in just a few days with the Protein Cleanse. Ideal for busy people and able to fit into any workout schedule, these ready-to-drink recipes make supporting your weight management goals as simple as it gets.</p><p>The Protein Cleanse:<br/>• Supports healthy weight management. </p><p>• Can help complement your workouts with healthy carbs and 38g of protein. </p><p>• Helps support your stamina and natural energy levels. </p><p>• May help reduce bloating and support muscle recovery. </p><p>• Supports gut health and digestion.</p><p> • Supports a healthy inflammatory response.<br/><br/><br/>Every sip is functional. Every bottle is nutritionist-designed to support your specific fitness and wellness goals.<br/><br/><br/><br/></p>",
            "open_by_default": false
          }
        },
        "accordion_UxFwnx": {
          "type": "accordion",
          "settings": {
            "title": "A Typical Day on a Juice Cleanse",
            "content": "<p>You’ll receive 3 juices and 3 smoothies for each day of your Protein Cleanse. We recommend starting around 8am and drinking one bottle at least every 2 hours, finishing the last bottle at 6pm.<br/><br/>Wake up & drink a large glass of water, have your coffee (if desired), and some fresh fruit.<br/><br/>8am: Sweet Greens Juice<br/> 10am: Citrus Carrot Juice<br/> 12 noon: Sweet Roots Juice<br/> 2pm: Chocolate Cashew Smoothie<br/> 4pm: Peanut Butter Smoothie<br/> 6pm: Vanilla Cashew Smoothie<br/><br/>For best results, we recommend drinking the juices in the first half of the day and the smoothies in the second half. This order is designed to support smoother digestion, help reduce occasional bloating, and complement your weight management goals.<br/><br/>EATING</p><p>Eat as much fresh fruit and vegetables as you desire throughout each day- either with your juices or in between. This includes baked, dry-roasted, or steamed potatoes. Instead of using oil or fats like butter on the potatoes, you can use lemon juice, salt, pepper, or any other fresh herbs and spices you like. Your Cleanse Guide includes a complete list of cleanse-approved foods and a recipe for a Hearty Vegetable Soup that you can enjoy without restriction during your cleanse.<br/><br/><br/>COFFEE<br/></p><p>We recommend that you drink your coffee either black or with a low-fat plant milk like oat milk. If you want to sweeten it, use honey. Adding sugar and creamer can work against your cleanse goals.<br/><br/><br/>DRINKING WATER<br/><br/>Even though these healthy juices are very hydrating, we strongly recommend drinking water throughout the day, ideally one glass between every bottle of juice. Water helps support your body's natural cleansing processes.<br/><br/><br/>EXERCISE<br/><br/>The Protein Cleanse is designed to support your workouts. With 38g of plant protein each day and adequate calories, you should be able to sustain your normal fitness routine. You can also eat foods from the cleanse-approved foods list if you feel you need additional calories.<br/><br/>SLEEP<br/><br/>Sleep is just as important to your wellness goals as what you eat. Getting quality rest supports your body's recovery during a cleanse. We recommend at least 7-9 hours each night.<br/><br/></p>",
            "open_by_default": false
          }
        },
